WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.160
We have an inalienable right to defend ourselves.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:13.330
A gun is just the tool to make the job easier.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.665
It's nothing for a white guy to walk up and
down the street with his rifle on his back.

00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:18.052
And everything's just fine.

00:00:18.052 --> 00:00:24.878
When a black person does it, we're a thug, we're an animal, we're about to go stick up a store or something.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:38.443
Locked and loaded.

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:48.670
Dead center.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.050
I shoot my guns every day.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:57.390
I train in hand to hand combat every day,
even by myself when no one's around, I train.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.309
Because it may save my life.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:06.873
But more importantly, it may save the lives
of whoever's with me.

00:01:06.873 --> 00:01:12.115
We are marching and organizing to build black
power in this city.

00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:18.680
To build black power in this city.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.060
When I talk to people in the African-American
community, I hear they want protection.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.659
There were some guys that came around and
they were shooting protesters, and the protestors

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:30.571
were saying that they were yelling some racial slurs.

00:01:30.571 --> 00:01:40.240
And that was when I decided to go back out
there.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.429
You have this history, well before the civil
war of organized black self-defense in 

00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:49.430
Northern communities where black people were free.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:54.490
In the post civil war period, the late 19th
and early 20th century you have state officials

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:58.610
who basically are in league with groups like
the Ku Klux Klan.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:06.568
I think that situation is mitigated to some
extent by the fact that black people

00:02:06.568 --> 00:02:14.376
 in the South, in fact, are armed and are able to defend
themselves.

00:02:14.376 --> 00:02:20.489
So there's a tremendous push in the 1950s
and 1960s for black voter registration.

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:25.271
We've got to make sure that they are reached
and get into the city to do the voting.

00:02:25.271 --> 00:02:31.370
The Ku Klux Klan basically decides that they're
going to go after the people who are registering

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:34.410
black voters, intimidate them and kill them.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:42.300
So you have groups are beginning to be formed,
designed to protect the black community and

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.920
protect civil rights workers who are registering
black voters.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.147
The most effective of these, I would argue
was a group called the Deacons for Defense and Justice.

00:02:51.147 --> 00:02:56.790
The Deacons for Defense and Justice were basically
black men who had been veterans of the second

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.180
world war or the Korean war.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:06.790
The Panthers were very good at publicity and
not particularly good at protecting black communities.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:12.858
The Deacons, on the other hand, just very silently let it be known, if you try to harm people in our community,

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:16.800
or the people working with us, it's not going to go very well for you.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.479
Defund the police.

00:03:18.479 --> 00:03:21.300
Defund the police.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.330
Defund the police.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.349
Defund the police.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:27.379
Defund the police.

00:03:27.379 --> 00:03:29.400
Defund the police.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.430
Defund the police.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.450
Defund the police.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:36.589
Defund the police.

00:03:36.589 --> 00:03:40.630
We have an inalienable right to defend ourselves.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:48.387
A gun is just something that I grab every
day and bring with me hoping that nothing would happen.

00:03:48.387 --> 00:03:54.408
But if it ever had to come to that situation,
then at least the option is open.

00:03:54.408 --> 00:03:55.590
Our streets.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.090
Our streets.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.269
Our streets.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.459
Our streets.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:03:59.650
Our streets.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.840
Our streets.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.030
Our streets.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.220
Our streets.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.480
I get the strangest looks when I walk around
looking like this.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.319
I get the strangest looks more from black
people than white people,

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:15.479
but then black people all of a sudden, you see pride just swell
up in their chest.

00:04:15.479 --> 00:04:27.227
When they see me walk around, like this. Like yes, yes he gets it. He knows that he has those rights too.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:52.550
You're at a protest that is talking about
the inequalities in a justice system and police brutality. 

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:59.830
And then you mentally have wired yourself to believe that only the cops should have the gun to protect you and other people.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.490
And I just thought that that was really ironic.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.450
Middle finger to the law.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.000
Middle finger to the law.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.140
But yet it's nothing for a white guy to walk
up and down the street with his rifle on his back.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:18.495
And everything's just fine. NRA, second amendment, it's like nothing.

00:05:18.495 --> 00:05:23.409
But when a black person does it, we're a thug, we're an animal. We're about to go stick up a store or something.

00:05:23.409 --> 00:05:32.846
But when you see these animals and thugs as
they like to call us, well armed, well-organized,

00:05:32.846 --> 00:05:37.691
yeah it makes you stop and think, yeah these
guns aren't just for the racist, the KKK,

00:05:37.691 --> 00:05:39.000
the Nazis or than anything else.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:46.555
These are also for those rogue police officers, those ones that like to brutalize us and harm us and get away with it. 

00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:49.867
No, we're not doing that anymore.

00:05:59.746 --> 00:06:03.877
My man, Eric Garner six years ago.

00:06:03.877 --> 00:06:07.677
Another reason why I had this hat made that
says I can't breathe.

00:06:07.677 --> 00:06:13.554
Because that's what he said when he was being
choked out by police for selling loose cigarettes.

00:06:13.554 --> 00:06:20.892
It's funny. I got the hat made six years after he said
it and six weeks after George Floyd said it.

00:06:20.892 --> 00:06:25.573
And there's the whole story about Philando
Castile right there.

00:06:25.573 --> 00:06:29.845
The baby was in the back seat. He's told them "I have a concealed weapons permit."

00:06:29.845 --> 00:06:31.410
"Show it to me."

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.831
He reaches for it and the man kills him.

00:06:34.831 --> 00:06:35.688
Kills him.

00:06:35.688 --> 00:06:38.448
Where was the NRA then?

00:06:38.448 --> 00:06:39.650
Silent.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:44.459
Didn't say a damn thing.

00:06:44.459 --> 00:06:52.610
When you walk around the statue and you see
pictures and birthdays and brief descriptions.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.420
How many more of the signs would you like
to see before it would change your mind that

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:07.970
maybe you're responsible for your own protection?

00:07:16.448 --> 00:07:21.156
One of the most frequent things that I've
always heard is that I would be killed by a cop.

00:07:21.156 --> 00:07:27.310
They believe that a cops perception of me
being armed is going to be the reason why I get shot.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:34.397
I can honestly say traffic stops prior to
me being armed are extremely different than when I am armed.

00:07:34.397 --> 00:07:42.031
And cops are a lot more friendly and a lot
more open to communication

00:07:42.031 --> 00:07:48.598
when the playing fields are the same.

00:07:48.598 --> 00:07:52.827
Everybody's out here, peaceful,
you know what I'm saying?

00:07:52.827 --> 00:07:56.305
Stop listening to the media, stop listening
to that sh*t. 

00:07:56.305 --> 00:07:58.516
We're out here singing song's about freedom.

00:07:58.516 --> 00:08:02.529
I can't wait 'till we don't live in a police state. 

00:08:02.529 --> 00:08:08.244
Ain't it great when we win? Ain't it great that we don't live in a police state.

00:08:08.244 --> 00:08:13.590
Almost a month ago, if you notice, wasn't
that many of us out there with guns.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:17.389
Now look at night, big difference right?

00:08:17.389 --> 00:08:18.389
Big difference.

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:21.250
We're peaceful, we're always going to be protected.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.330
And that's been my mission.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:28.071
I believe that I'm channeling my ancestors. I'm channeling activists before.

00:08:28.071 --> 00:08:33.436
The police are violent. We will not be silent.

00:08:33.436 --> 00:08:39.330
You had in the sixties and before, a situation
where there was little or no help from the

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.630
federal government in protecting your civil
rights.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.350
That's not the case today.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:48.300
There's still the issue of how well are you
protected?

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:53.241
Do you want to totally surrender your ability
to protect yourself to others?

00:08:53.241 --> 00:08:57.137
Basic question, is it a good thing to be helpless?

00:08:57.137 --> 00:09:05.957
And I say, no.

